node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Agent machinery, not project state. `.claude/worktrees/` holds a FULL CHECKOUT of this repository
# per isolated subagent — so with a catch-all `git add -A`, one of them lands inside the repo as a
# nested copy. Added 2026-08-07 the same day the first isolated worktree was created and before any
# commit swept it up; every commit that day used `git add -A`, so the next one would have.
.claude/

# Build output. Generated by `npm run build` and read into memory at startup by loadDist — it is
# derived, it is content-hashed per build, and committing it means every build produces a diff of
# renamed binaries. Added after four dist files were committed by accident.
app/dist/
app/dist-server/

# The BROWSER SUITE's own build, and the separation is the point rather than tidiness.
#
# The harness used to run `npm run build`, which writes the two directories above — the same ones
# the launchd server loads at startup. So a test run replaced the running product's bundle, and a
# restart during one served whatever the suite had last built. That is not theoretical: on
# 2026-08-22 the operator spent a day on a build a test run had left behind, with two controls dead,
# and the fix was a rebuild.
#
# Worse than a stale build: mutation testing deliberately breaks the source and rebuilds to prove a
# test catches it. A restart at that moment serves code broken on purpose.
app/dist-e2e/
app/dist-server-e2e/

# Runtime state from a locally-run server. It carries the session TOKENS the server prints
# at startup, plus a registry of real absolute paths and a request log — none of which is source,
# and all of which would otherwise be committed. Found 2026-08-31 sitting untracked-but-not-ignored
# at the repository root, having survived a secrets sweep that EXCLUDED it as a local artefact.
.preview-state/

app/test-results/
app/playwright-report/
app/.vite/

# The workbench's own server state — see WORKBENCH-ONLY.md. Kept inside the checkout so it cannot
# be confused with the running installation's `~/.soil-viewer`.
app/.workbench-state/

# The harness's sampled corpus — regenerated from the mock soil by `npm run harness:corpus`, never
# source. `probes/` IS source and stays committed: it is the hand-built half of the denominator, one
# fixture per markdown construct, and coverage there is guaranteed rather than sampled.
app/test/harness/corpus/

# The census artefacts the same command writes beside the corpus. **Every record in them is an
# ABSOLUTE PATH of the scanned tree**, so they carry the scanning machine's home directory and
# username — 1,644 occurrences of it in one run here. They are derived, they regenerate in seconds,
# and they were untracked-but-not-ignored until 2026-08-31, which is precisely how the runtime state
# directory nearly shipped a fortnight of session tokens. Ignoring the corpus directory alone was not
# enough; these are its siblings.
app/test/harness/manifest.json
app/test/harness/tree-counts.json
app/test/harness/tree-records.json
